	(text "I2C ADDRESS (7-bit): hard-wired. Populate ONE 10K resistor per address bit.\nADDR1 ADDR0 : address\n0     0     : 0x28\n0     1     : 0x29\n1     0     : 0x2A\n1     1     : 0x2B"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.686 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "66553d2f-352a-47f0-b8f7-01dfdf229263")
	)
	(text "24.576 MHz, CL = 12 pF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 264.795 111.125 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "74bd036d-dada-4686-a4f3-fb4e6d5ae38a")
	)
	(text "POWER: J1 supplies +3V3 only. U2 (TLV75518, 1.8V) feeds AVDD, HPVDD, IOVDD and REG_EN (all +1V8).\nDigital I/O (I2C, I2S, PD_N) is 1.8V logic - NOT 3.3V tolerant.\nI2C pull-ups R1/R2 (4.7k) go to +1V8 from U2. Remove R1/R2 if the host provides its own pull-ups.\nSELFBOOT is hard-wired low by R5 (no EEPROM self-boot). PD_N is pulled high by R6.\nUnused digital pins (BCLK_1, FSYNC_1, SDATAI_1, SDATAO_1, DMIC_CLK0/1) are left unconnected;\nenable the codec's internal pull-downs on the input-capable ones in firmware.\nClock: on-board crystal Y1 (24.576 MHz) only; no external MCLK."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.096 98.806 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a9711bbf-2faa-4d54-b0ea-8cd6dad570e3")
	)
